  "_commit": {
    "id": "03385c83263afc259176080d7cfdfb0868a3cba2",
    "author": "Matthew Smith <matthew.smith@ki.se>",
    "committer": "Matthew Smith <matthew.smith@ki.se>",
    "message": "Version 0.99.12: draw report figures with cairo on Windows\n\nOn Windows, png() defaults to the GDI device, which holds about 15 GDI\nobjects for every plot drawn on it until the device closes. knitr keeps one\ndevice open per chunk, and the ion-image chunk draws four images per\nfeature, so a study of a few dozen features reached Windows' limit of\n10,000 GDI objects per process and the render stopped with \"processing of\nthe plot ran out of memory\" (028 IgE, 35 features, R 4.6.2). The cairo\ndevice holds none: 100 plots in one chunk left 1,347 GDI objects with the\ndefault device and 14 with cairo.\n\nThe report now sets dev.args = list(type = \"cairo\") on Windows unless the\ncaller set dev.args already, and the two heatmaps that open their own\ndevice take the same type, so every figure is drawn the same way. Other\nplatforms already default to cairo or Quartz and are unchanged.\n\nNEWS: the release section is now 0.99.12.\n",
    "time": 1794325621
  },
